            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for a publication, then the Russian for a print run."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: преступление",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "преступление (prestupléniye) — \"a crime\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Это было серьёзное преступление. Éto býlo seryóznoye prestupléniye. It was a serious crime."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter. Совершить преступление (prestupléniye) — to commit a crime."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "преступление (prestupléniye) is built on преступить \"to step over (the law)\", from пре-, the Church Slavonic shape of native пере-, and ступить \"to step\", the root of ступень, Proto-Slavic stǫpenĭ (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
